Third-party projects referenced
-------------------------------

Nothing from any project below is bundled in, linked against, or redistributed
by this crate. They are named because the crate's documentation, tests and
comparison fixtures refer to them, and because naming a project you compare
yourself to is the honest thing to do. Each is the property of its authors; no
endorsement is implied in either direction.

* SPARK, SPARK Pro and gnatprove -- AdaCore. The workflow this crate is
  modelled on (contracts in the source, proofs discharged by a tool). This
  crate is an independent experiment and is not affiliated with, sponsored by,
  or supported by AdaCore.
* Z3 -- Microsoft Research. Used as a differential *oracle* in the test suite
  (`tests/oracle.rs`, `examples/z3diff.rs`), invoked as a subprocess. Not a
  dependency of the crate.
* Kani -- Kani Rust Verifier project. Differential oracle, invoked as a
  subprocess. Not a dependency.
* Verus -- Verus project. Differential oracle, invoked as a subprocess. Not a
  dependency.
* Prusti -- ETH Zurich. Referenced in the comparison fixtures only; not run by
  the test suite and not a dependency.
* MIRAI -- Meta. Referenced in documentation only; not a dependency.
* Lean 4 -- Lean FRO. Differential oracle, invoked as a subprocess. Not a
  dependency.
* Coq -- Inria and contributors. Differential oracle, invoked as a subprocess.
  Not a dependency.
* CBMC -- used indirectly by Kani; not a dependency of this crate.
* Ferrocene -- Ferrocene project. The *qualified* toolchain, used by an optional
  build gate when a subscription is configured. Not a dependency.
* rustc_public / `rustc-dev` -- the Rust project. Used by `tools/mir-oracle`, an
  excluded workspace member that is never published and never a dependency.

The crate itself depends on nothing outside this repository. `scripts/gate.sh`
step 5 enforces that, so this section cannot drift from the manifests.
